bours in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"incidentEdges"},{"text":" order. O(n + m).","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule":{"role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule","url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule","title":"ColoringModule","type":"topic","abstract":[],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://ColoringModule/s8SendableP":{"type":"unresolvable","title":"Swift.Sendable","identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/s8SendableP"},"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule/ColoringStrategy":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/ColoringStrategy","title":"ColoringStrategy","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ColoringStrategy"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/coloringstrategy","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"How "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"greedyColoring(strategy:)"},{"type":"text","text":" orders the vertices. Each vertex in turn takes the least colour"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"none of its already coloured neighbours has (first fit). Degrees are simple degrees (distinct"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"other neighbours, self-loops left out); ties go to the lesser vertex index, except for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".coloredNeighbors"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ColoringStrategy"}]},"doc://ColoringModule/SQ":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/SQ","type":"unresolvable","title":"Swift.Equatable"},"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule/ColoringStrategy/independentSet":{"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/ColoringStrategy\/independentSet","url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/coloringstrategy\/independentset","title":"ColoringStrategy.independentSet","fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"independentSet","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Colour classes one at a time: class k is a maximal independent set of the vertices not yet","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"coloured, built by repeatedly taking the one with the fewest neighbours among those still","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"available (the least index on ties) and making it and its neighbours unavailable.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"O(χ (n + m) log n) for χ classes.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule/ColoringStrategy/Equatable-Implementations":{"abstract":[],"role":"collectionGroup","title":"Equatable Implementations","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/coloringstrategy\/equatable-implementations","identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/ColoringStrategy\/Equatable-Implementations","kind":"article"},"doc://ColoringModule/SH":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/SH","type":"unresolvable","title":"Swift.Hashable"},"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule/ColoringStrategy/saturationLargestFirst":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"saturationLargestFirst"}],"abstract":[{"text":"DSatur (Brélaz 1979): first a vertex of greatest degree, then repeatedly the uncoloured","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertex with the most distinct colours among its neighbours, ties to the greatest degree in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the whole graph, then to the lesser index. Exact on bipartite graphs. O((n + m) log n).","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","title":"ColoringStrategy.saturationLargestFirst","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/coloringstrategy\/saturationlargestfirst","identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/ColoringStrategy\/saturationLargestFirst","kind":"symbol"},"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule/ColoringStrategy/coloredNeighbors":{"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/ColoringStrategy\/coloredNeighbors","url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/coloringstrategy\/coloredneighbors","title":"ColoringStrategy.coloredNeighbors","fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"coloredNeighbors","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"First the vertex of greatest degree (the least index on ties), then repeatedly the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"uncoloured vertex with the most coloured neighbours. Ties among those fall as a two-way","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"indexed binary max-heap breaks them, not by index: vertices are pushed in index order and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"raised neighbour by neighbour in ascending order; an entry moves above an equal parent and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sinks to the left child unless the right one is strictly greater. O((n + m) log n).","type":"text"}]},"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule/ColoringStrategy/smallestLast":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/ColoringStrategy\/smallestLast","title":"ColoringStrategy.smallestLast","fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"smallestLast","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/coloringstrategy\/smallestlast","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Matula–Beck: repeatedly remove a vertex of least degree in what is left (the least index on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ties), then colour in the reverse of that removal order. At most degeneracy + 1 colours, so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"at most 6 on a planar graph. O((n + m) log n).","type":"text"}]},"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule/ColoringStrategy/connectedSequentialDepthFirst":{"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/ColoringStrategy\/connectedSequentialDepthFirst","url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/coloringstrategy\/connectedsequentialdepthfirst","title":"ColoringStrategy.connectedSequentialDepthFirst","fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"connectedSequentialDepthFirst","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The same in depth-first preorder. O(n + m)."}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule/ColoringStrategy/largestFirst":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"largestFirst"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Degree descending, the lesser index first on ties: Welsh–Powell, which colours class by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"class in this order and gives the same colouring as first fit. O(n + m).","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","title":"ColoringStrategy.largestFirst","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/coloringstrategy\/largestfirst","identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/ColoringStrategy\/largestFirst","kind":"symbol"}}}